FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/interpreter.rs:416 — `module_path` checks `Path::new(path).exists()` and `module_source` uses `std::fs`, bypassing `vfs` — the memory filesystem `files.write` writes to on wasm is invisible here, so write-then-import succeeds natively and fails as `Cannot find module` in the playground, contradicting `src/vfs.rs:28` (`Every path into the filesystem goes through here`); same bypass at `src/bytecode/vm.rs:3379` and `src/bytecode/vm.rs:3667` — route both lookups and reads through `crate::vfs::exists` / `crate::vfs::read_to_string`.
2. [MAJOR] src/wasm.rs:758 — `rb_run_into` refuses null-buffer-with-nonzero-cap but silently accepts non-null-buffer-with-null-cell, skipping the copy and returning success with the output discarded — a host lending a buffer with no length gets `0` and no bytes — add the mirror refusal (`!output.is_null() && output_len.is_null()` → `-1`, same for error).
3. [MAJOR] src/wasm.rs:431 — `copy_out` uses `copy_nonoverlapping` for a host-supplied `dest` that may alias the channel (e.g. a prior `rb_output_ptr` passed back as `dest`), which is UB on overlap — use `std::ptr::copy` (memmove) for the host copy.
4. [MINOR] wasm/redblue.js:234 — `readChannel` calls `rb_release(scratch)` before creating the `Uint8Array` view and decoding it, reading a buffer after releasing it; works only because release merely marks free without clearing on a single thread — decode/copy out of `scratch` first, then release.
5. [MINOR] src/lib.rs:545 — `print_version` hardcodes `Redblue v0.1.0` while `Cargo.toml:3` is `0.2.0` and the new `src/wasm.rs:270` `version()` reports `CARGO_PKG_VERSION`, so native `rb version` and playground `version()` disagree — print `env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")`.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
